<%# GET /xeraen/bio — the long-form record as a console screen
    (2026-10-28; the eight stacked glowing fieldsets are gone): a bar,
    "// SECTION //" rules, 16/20 prose, status rows for the transmitter
    readouts, the LATEST TRANSMISSION track row, the closing quote,
    destination rows and the "> " prompt. data-boot="done" + autofocus
    off: no line reveal, and the prompt never steals the keyboard from
    scrolling. bio-credit replays the bio_viewed achievement POST the
    React page fired on mount for logged-in viewers. %>
<% content_for :title, "XERAEN Bio — hackr.tv" %>
<% current_year = Date.current.year %>
<% future_year = current_year + 100 %>

<%= render layout: "shared/default_chrome", locals: {ascii: false} do %>
  <div class="console console--xeraen xt-bio" data-controller="terminal bio-credit" data-boot="done"
       data-terminal-autofocus-value="false" data-bio-credit-slug-value="xeraen">
    <div class="console-bar">
      <h1 class="console-bar-title">XERAEN</h1>
      <span class="console-bar-sub">OPERATIVE RECORD · BIO</span>
      <span class="console-bar-right">
        <%= link_to "[<] XERAEN", "/xeraen", class: "console-bar-link" %>
        <%= link_to "[>] RELEASES", "/xeraen/releases", class: "console-bar-link" %>
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// FIRST CONTACT //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p><%= codex_text("Before the broadcasts. Before The.CyberPul.se. Before the [[The Fracture Network|Fracture Network]] had a voice.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-lead">There was just a signal. Reaching backward. Seeking to be heard.</p>
      <p>
        XERAEN doesn't perform. XERAEN transmits. Every track is a frequency aimed at a point in
        spacetime that shouldn't be reachable. Music transmitted through temporal displacement. The sound, a message
        in a bottle thrown into the electromagnetic ocean between centuries.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-brand">You're not listening to songs. You're intercepting communications.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// LATEST TRANSMISSION //</span></div>
    <% if @latest_featured_track %>
      <%= render "artist_pages/embedded_track", track: @latest_featured_track %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="xt-tuning">[TUNING SIGNAL...]</p>
    <% end %>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// SOLO TRANSMISSIONS //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p>
        Where The.CyberPul.se broadcasts the resistance, XERAEN's solo work traces an evolution.
        The early transmissions burned hot - hardcore punk aggression, metalcore fury, the raw
        voltage of someone screaming into the void hoping the past would hear.
      </p>
      <p>
        But transmissions change over distance. What started as a sonic assault has transformed into
        something XERAEN calls <span class="xt-brand">OMNIWAVE</span> -
        every frequency at once. It's an amalgamation of everything that ever moved him, rhythmic
        guitars weaving through synthesized atmospheres until genre boundaries dissolve. It
        plays as collage: covers of songs, reinterpretations of other Fracture Network bands, even
        old video game scores pulled from the deep archive, all filtered through XERAEN's temporal
        emanations and broadcast back familiar yet displaced. Between the covers run his own
        compositions - some tightly structured, some pure atmosphere - painting a sweeping image
        of life and emotion in the 22nd century.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-brand">From hardcore fury to OMNIWAVE frequencies - the sound evolves, but the signal never stops.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE TRANSMITTER //</span></div>
    <div class="console-status">
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">ORIGIN</span><span class="console-val"><%= future_year %></span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">DESTINATION</span><span class="console-val"><%= current_year %></span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">STATUS</span><span class="console-val"><span class="xt-brand">BROADCASTING</span></span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">COST</span><span class="console-val">EVERYTHING</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p><%= codex_text("In #{future_year}, XERAEN operates alone. [[The Fracture Network]] has cells, bands, operatives - but someone has to sit at the console. Someone has to hold the frequency. Someone has to keep transmitting to the ones who decoded it and wrote back across a hundred years - the ones he can reach but never stand beside.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-dim">
        The solo work comes from those hours. The space between coordinated operations. The quiet
        moments when the only company is the hum of equipment and the impossible distance between
        now and then.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// WHAT THE SIGNAL CARRIES //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE STATIC DECODED</h3>
      <p>
        The interference isn't noise - it's the sound of a signal fighting through a hundred years
        of temporal resistance. Every crackle, every dropout, every moment of distortion is
        evidence of the distance traveled. XERAEN leaves it in. The static is part of the message.
      </p>
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] FREQUENCIES OF ABSENCE</h3>
      <p>
        Music about what's missing. The people who won't exist if the mission succeeds. The
        timeline that collapses when victory is achieved. The version of yourself that has to
        be sacrificed. These aren't sad songs - they're honest ones. This is what it sounds like
        to accept the cost.
      </p>
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE WAVEFORM OF LOVE</h3>
      <p><%= codex_text("[[Ashlinn]] exists in #{current_year}. XERAEN exists in #{future_year}. The only way to touch across that distance is through frequency. Every transmission is a love letter encoded in electromagnetic radiation. Every track is proof that some connections don't require shared spacetime.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-brand">"I can't hold you. So I send you sound waves instead. I hope they feel like what I meant."</p>
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE WEIGHT OF THE CONSOLE</h3>
      <p>
        Someone has to stay. Someone has to keep the frequency open while others fight, infiltrate,
        resist. XERAEN chose the console. Chose to be the voice rather than the fist. Chose
        transmission over action. These tracks are what that choice sounds like - the profound
        isolation of being the one who stays behind and broadcasts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE ERASURE //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p>Here's what XERAEN knows that the listeners don't fully understand:</p>
      <p><%= codex_text("Every successful operation brings the end closer. Every [[GovCorp]] system that falls, every mind that awakens, every node that joins the network - all of it accelerates the timeline toward collapse. Toward a future where [[GovCorp]] never rises. Where the #{future_year} XERAEN broadcasts from never exists.") %></p>
      <p>
        The solo work is a countdown. Each transmission potentially the last. Each one sent
        with the knowledge that success means silence.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-brand">Victory is extinction. XERAEN broadcasts anyway.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE PARADOX OF PRESENCE //</span></div>
    <div class="console-status">
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">TEMPORAL STATUS</span><span class="console-val">UNSTABLE</span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">EXISTENCE</span><span class="console-val">CONDITIONAL</span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">SIGNAL</span><span class="console-val"><span class="xt-brand">PERSISTENT</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p>
        If you're hearing this, the paradox holds. XERAEN still exists in <%= future_year %>, still
        holds the frequency, still sends transmissions backward through the century. The future
        hasn't changed yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        But every listen is a variable. Every new receiver shifts the equation. Every mind that
        tunes in brings the collapse closer.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-dim">
        XERAEN's solo work is simultaneously a plea to keep listening and an acknowledgment that
        listening enough will end the transmission forever.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// LAST WORDS //</span></div>
    <blockquote class="xt-quote">
      <p>I broadcast from a future I'm trying to prevent.</p>
      <p>I send love letters to someone I'll never meet if we win.</p>
      <p>I make music that documents my own eventual non-existence.</p>
      <p class="xt-quote-gap">The signal is all I have. It was never mine.</p>
      <p>When I stop, it won't.</p>
      <p class="xt-quote-gap">But you'll remember the frequency.</p>
      <p>Somewhere in the static, I'll still be reaching for you.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="xt-sig">— XERAEN <span class="console-dim">· transmitting from <%= future_year %> · for as long as <%= future_year %> exists</span></p>

    <%= render "artist_pages/console_destinations", artist: "xeraen", except: "BIO" %>
    <%= render "shared/console_prompt", hint: console_prompt_hint("xeraen", except: "BIO") %>
  </div>
<% end %>
